{"id":"3e6a8ce23a814b62ae38993394669d8e","owner":"NGS.GIS_noaa","ownerId":"8af989516950467288944e3e4ba0375e","orgId":"C8EMgrsFcRFL6LrL","created":1716237389000,"modified":1790002923000,"guid":null,"name":"Alpha_SPCS2022_Multizone_Complete_Zones_Feature_Layer_View","title":"Beta SPCS2022 Multizone Complete Zones Feature Layer View","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service","View Service"],"description":"<span><p style='margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt;'><span style='font-size:11pt; font-family:Arial; color:#000000; background-color:transparent; font-weight:400; font-style:normal; font-variant:normal; text-decoration:none;'>NOAA\u2019s\n National Geodetic Survey (NGS) is in the process of modernizing the \nNational Spatial Reference System (NSRS).  As part of NSRS \nModernization, the State Plane Coordinate System (SPCS) will be updated \nto SPCS2022.  This Feature Layer View displays the Multizone Complete Zones \nfrom the SPCS2022 zone layers.  This layer is intended for \nNGS customers, stakeholders, partners, and other constituents to view \nand provide feedback on the SPCS2022 zones that are planned for \nrelease. These zones are beta and should not be considered the final definitions. <br /><\/span><\/p><p style='margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt;'><br /><\/p><p style='margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt;'><a href='https://noaa.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=dddb7bc0be6f4e56a1c370c8d529d1a0' style='text-decoration-line:none;' rel='nofollow ugc'><span style='font-size:11pt; font-family:Arial; color:rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color:transparent; font-variant-numeric:normal; font-variant-east-asian:normal; font-variant-alternates:normal; text-decoration-line:underline;'>Beta SPCS2022 Experience<\/span><\/a><\/p><p style='margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt;'><a href='https://noaa.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=ddd132cf6dc84a8c9b2c6e73bf8e4923' style='text-decoratio